              "json": "## About the data and limitations\r\n\r\n### Sources\r\n\r\n| Data | Source |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| VM size, region, zone, availability set, OS, priority | `microsoft.compute/virtualmachines` |\r\n| VMSS size, capacity, orchestration and upgrade mode | `microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets` |\r\n| Autoscale minimum and maximum | `microsoft.insights/autoscalesettings` |\r\n| Customer-visible advisories | `ServiceHealthResources` |\r\n\r\n### Important semantics\r\n\r\n* Capacity limitation is **not** a shutdown notice for active v3/v4 VMs.\r\n* Several older families also have separate retirement dates and are marked\r\n  **Capacity restricted + retirement scheduled**.\r\n* The workbook reports deployed inventory and configured VMSS growth. It cannot\r\n  guarantee quota approval or regional/zone capacity.\r\n* Recommended target families are directional. Exact target SKU selection requires\r\n  workload sizing and live quota/capacity validation.\r\n\r\n### Coverage limits\r\n\r\nThe workbook directly covers Compute VMs and VM scale sets indexed by Resource Graph.\r\nManaged-service compute that does not expose a VM/VMSS resource in the selected\r\nsubscription, and service-specific pools such as Azure Batch pools, can require\r\nadditional service APIs.\r\n\r\n### Explicit affected series\r\n\r\nF, Fs, Fsv2; D, Ds, Dv2, Dsv2, Dv3, Dsv3, Dv4, Dsv4, Ddv4, Ddsv4,\r\nDav4, Dasv4; B, Bs, Av2, Amv2; Ev3, Esv3, Ev4, Esv4, Edv4, Edsv4,\r\nEav4, Easv4; G, Gs; Ls and Lsv2."
